# A loop of mandatory actions that puts a counter on a permanent each time round never comes back to the same position, and
# still has no way to stop: the game is a draw (CR 104.4b). Bot2 has Chainsaw ("Whenever one or more creatures die, put a rev
# counter on this Equipment"), cast on turn 4 with no creature for its enters ability to damage. On turn 5 Bot1 animates
# its Entombed Worldgorger Dragon and the loop of the draw scenarios begins, every step of it forced; each time Animate
# Dead's leaves ability sacrifices the Dragon, Chainsaw's ability, Bot2's alone, puts a rev counter on it. The counters only
# grow: nothing reads them but Chainsaw's own "+X/+0" for a creature it equips, and it equips none, and no rule ends anything
# by them. So round after round the board is the same but for one more counter, no player can do anything but pass, and
# nothing will ever be different: the loop goes round until the rules judge it endless, and the game is a draw - not a game
# that never ends. (How many counters Chainsaw has then is the engine's to say, not the rules': the rules only make it a
# draw.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Entomb
Animate Dead
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Worldgorger Dragon
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Chainsaw
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Entomb.Cast
Bot1.Search(Worldgorger Dragon)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Chainsaw.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield = Mountain; Mountain; Chainsaw
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Animate Dead.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Worldgorger Dragon)

[Expect]
Result = Draw
DrawReason = MandatoryLoop
Bot1.Status = (absent)
Bot2.Status = (absent)
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
Turn = 5
Step = Main1
